<task id="056" project="unified-access-control-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Register sprk_todo / sprk_event / sprk_communication as scoped child modules (FR-27)</title>
    <phase>3 Child inheritance</phase>
    <gate>blocked — requires 055 (inheritance term) + 009 (FR-08 scoped todo PATCH) + 018 (FR-17 in-clause bound) merged; amended 2026-09-30: also 134 (column allow-list), 135 (CIAM veto parity), 147 (memo taxonomy + stamps)</gate>
    <status>pending</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Authorization-path .cs: module descriptors define what external callers can query; the periphery (Tier-1 codes, grid-config allow-list) is security-adjacent.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Originally sonnet (descriptor registration mirrors the shipped documents/invoices descriptors). Raised to opus by the 2026-09-30 amendment: the scope now includes CIAM exposure of five child modules, new external write routes on matters/work assignments, veto parity on both planes and the sprk_relatedproject access decision — an authorization-boundary change where a wrong dim or gate discloses a secure record's children to contacts.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>phase3-wave5</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Touches Infrastructure/DI/ExternalAccessModule.cs + Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ModuleEntitlementResolver.cs — inside the exclusive ExternalAccess zone. Amended 2026-09-30: also Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalProjectDataEndpoints.cs + Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ExternalDataService.cs (matter/WA event routes) — also edited by tasks 146 and 152, and ExternalAccessModule.cs by 134 and 148: serialize; whichever runs second rebases.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>055, 009, 018, 134, 135, 147 (134/135/147 added by the 2026-09-30 amendment: 134 = analysis column allow-list, 135 = CIAM veto parity needed by amendment 8(e), 147 = sprk_memo taxonomy + memo stamp backfill needed by amendment 8(a))</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth, dataverse, testing</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-4 hours as originally scoped; ~12-18 hours with the 2026-09-30 amendments (five modules, matter/WA event routes, CIAM exposure, relatedproject decision, possible amendment-7 parity routes)</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Register the three child modules (todos, events, communications) on the external fetch seam with scope dimensions over the THREE externally-grantable core-ancestor stamp columns (project / matter / workassignment — NOT service request; see the constraint) — and close every peripheral cost investigation 01 §7 enumerated: metadata-verify the regarding logical names, extend Tier-1 entitlement module codes, extend the grid-configuration allow-list, and document the client fetch-column projection requirement. This is NOT "just descriptors" — treat the periphery as first-class scope.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. External-access module registry, FetchXML scope injection, Tier-1 entitlements. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>Three new ExternalModuleDescriptor registrations (dims: sprk_regardingproject / sprk_regardingmatter / sprk_regardingworkassignment as they exist per entity, verified against live metadata — NO service-request dim, because no accessible-service-request set exists on CallerPrincipal to scope against); Tier-1 module codes wired for workforce and CIAM per the shipped policy; grid-config ids added where widget configs exist; seam tests proving scoped fetch, record 403 behaviour, and fail-closed empty-set handling.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>spec.md FR-27. Investigation 01 §7: descriptor mirroring ExternalAccessModule.cs:166-176 is the small part; the six real costs are (1) client FetchXML must project every dim column or ScopeRows drops rows fail-closed; (2) Tier-1 CIAM blanket set is exactly { assigned-work } — new module codes need OutsideCounselModules and/or sprk_approlemodulemap rows; (3) grid-configuration static allow-list needs each new widget config id; (4) only the composed root sets can be dims, and there are exactly THREE (project / matter / workassignment) — 054 does NOT add a fourth, contrary to this file's original text; (5) IN-list fan-out (bounded by Phase 0 FR-17); (6) the seam is read-only — the unscoped PATCH /todos/{id} was fixed by Phase 0 FR-08 and MUST NOT be reused as a write pattern. Only sprk_todo.sprk_regardingproject is code-verified — every other regarding logical name must be checked against live metadata before wiring.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/ExternalAccessModule.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ModuleEntitlementResolver.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalModuleDataEndpoints.cs (the seam being extended — read, do not modify)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ExternalModuleRegistry.cs (ScopeRows fail-closed re-filter)</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ + tests/integration/seam/ (module scope tests)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="055" status="pending">Inheritance term so scoped rows carry correct rights.</dependency>
      <dependency task="009" status="completed">FR-08 scoped todo PATCH — todos must not become a child module while an unscoped write exists.</dependency>
      <dependency task="018" status="completed">FR-17 bounded in-clause in Tier2ScopeFilterInjector (06 §F3) — without it the new modules break for high-membership users.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Fail closed: unregistered entities stay 403; all-empty dims stay 200-with-0-rows-no-query; scope: descriptor wiring must not alter the seam's deny paths.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Scope dimensions may reference ONLY the THREE composed externally-grantable core root sets (project / matter / workassignment). 🔴 A `sprk_regardingservicerequest` dim is FORBIDDEN even where the column exists: a ScopeDimension can only point at a set that exists on the principal, and there is deliberately no accessible-service-request set (owner ruling 2026-09-09, task 028 — a service request is core but never externally grantable). Service-request scoping runs through the SEPARATE, already-shipped `service-requests` module, which scopes by `sprk_requestedby` and is plane-gated. Adding a child-entity accessible set is likewise forbidden (06 §F1 2-hop trap) — a todo regarding only a communication is reachable because FR-26 stamped its core ancestor, not because a communication set exists. Scope: descriptor definitions.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Every dim's logical name MUST be verified against live Dataverse metadata (mcp or Web API $metadata) before registration; record the verification table in notes. Scope: all three descriptors.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-03">Result caps must be visible: confirm the module pageSize + the FR-17 bound surface the "Only 5,000 records displayed" style message contract for these modules; scope: descriptor pageSize decisions, documented.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md-§10">Placement justification in PR citing .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md; publish size ≤ 60 MB reported. Scope: PR description.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>external module registry + scope injection</topic>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-003-authorization-seams.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/investigation/01-spa-plane.md</file>
      <file>projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/investigation/06-adversarial-critique.md</file>
      <file>docs/architecture/spaarke-todo-architecture.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="uac-access-control" location=".claude/patterns/auth/uac-access-control.md">Seam map.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Context + rigor declaration.</step>
    <step order="1">Metadata verification: for sprk_todo, sprk_event, sprk_communication, list which of the three externally-grantable core-ancestor lookup columns exist (logical names, exact); write the table to notes. Any missing column shrinks that module's dims — never guess.</step>
    <step order="2">Register the three descriptors mirroring the invoices descriptor (ExternalAccessModule.cs:181-190 as-merged), dims per the verification table. 🔴 Do NOT add a service-request dim even where the column exists — see the constraint; that instruction was in this file in error and is retired.</step>
    <step order="3">Tier-1: add module codes per the shipped policy — decide workforce (sprk_approlemodulemap data + code constant) and CIAM (OutsideCounselModules) exposure explicitly; default to NOT adding CIAM exposure unless the spec's Type-3 story requires it, and record the decision.</step>
    <step order="4">Grid-config allow-list: add config ids ONLY for widgets that exist today; if none exist yet for these modules, record that the id must be added when the widget ships (do not pre-add placeholder ids).</step>
    <step order="5">Tests: per module — scoped fetch returns only rows whose stamp is in the caller's root sets; record GET on a child id 403s (by design); caller with zero roots gets 0 rows with no Dataverse query; fetch not projecting the dim column drops rows (fail-closed over-hide pinned as EXPECTED behaviour with the projection requirement documented).</step>
    <step order="6">Build + tests green; publish size reported. Update TASK-INDEX.md; write the metadata table + Tier-1 decisions to projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/phase3-child-modules.md.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If sprk_event or sprk_communication lacks ALL THREE externally-grantable core-ancestor columns in live metadata (no usable stamp target exists — a service-request column alone does NOT count, since it cannot be a dim), STOP and escalate — that entity cannot be a scoped child module until schema adds the stamp columns, which is an owner decision, not a task improvisation.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>ExternalModuleDescriptor registry (Infrastructure/DI/ExternalAccessModule.cs:146-246) — the documents/invoices descriptors are the exact pattern; no todo/event/communication module is registered (Register throws on duplicates; grep confirms absence).</existing>
    <extension>Yes — this IS the extension path: new descriptors on the existing registry, no new mechanism (055's inheritance term supplied the model generalization the critique demanded; 054 does NOT supply a fourth root set — that premise was retired).</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>FR-27 acceptance fails: a contact with Project 1 access cannot see its events, communications or To Dos on the SPA at all (no external read path exists for those entities today — investigation 01 §7).</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/ExternalAccessModule.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ModuleEntitlementResolver.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ + tests/integration/seam/ (module scope tests)</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/phase3-child-modules.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a caller with Project P in their root set, a todos-module fetch returns todos stamped sprk_regardingproject = P (including todos whose direct regarding is a communication under P, via the FR-26 stamp).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a caller with zero accessible roots, each new module's fetch returns 0 rows with NO Dataverse query issued.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a fetch referencing another entity in link-entity is rejected (guard regression pin); a record GET for a child row 403s.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a caller not entitled to the module's Tier-1 code does not see the module in entitlements (and CIAM exposure matches the recorded decision).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The metadata-verification table in notes lists every dim column with its live logical name; no descriptor contains an unverified name.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Build + tests green; publish size ≤ 60 MB reported.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>spec.md FR-27; investigation 01 §7 costs 1-6 are the checklist. Client widgets consuming these modules are downstream (SPA-r3 project) — this task's deliverable is the server seam + documented projection contract.</notes>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>

  <amendments date="2026-09-30" source="owner C10 part 2 decision (session 27, rounds 1-2): children of a record must have 'the same contact access as the main record'">
    <verdict>SCOPE EXTENDED. Status unchanged. The owner ruled (session27 note, C10 + round 2 item 6 "contact coverage for children") that documents, communications, memos, events, to-dos and every other child of a record carry the SAME contact access as the main record, on every root type. Contacts reach children through app-only reads keyed on the parent, so Dataverse ownership (tasks 146-149) does not give them access — this task's module seam and the external routes do. Coverage measured 2026-09-30 (session27 note, C10 research): documents project/matter/work assignment; invoices yes; to-dos yes; events PROJECT ONLY; communications, memos, analyses NONE. The amendments below close every gap; they are in scope here, not follow-ups (owner: no scope cuts, nothing deferred).</verdict>
    <amendment n="1">EVENTS ON MATTERS AND WORK ASSIGNMENTS. The events module's dims cover all three roots (sprk_regardingproject / sprk_regardingmatter / sprk_regardingworkassignment, metadata-verified per step 1). ALSO the external event ROUTES are project-only today: `Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalProjectDataEndpoints.cs:202` (GET /projects/{id}/events) and `:210` (POST), backed by `Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/ExternalDataService.cs` `GetEventsAsync` :560 (project filter) and `CreateEventAsync` :579 (binds `sprk_RegardingProject@odata.bind` only, :596). Add the matter and work-assignment equivalents by mirroring the shipped to-do routes (`:147-169`, GET/POST /matters/{id}/todos and /workassignments/{id}/todos, which already generalize the root binding via `TodoRootBinding`) — same gate shape, same rights requirement (Create needs the caller's Collaborate-or-higher on THAT root, exactly as the project route). Justification (CLAUDE.md §11): existing = the project event routes + the matter/WA to-do routes; extension = generalize `CreateEventAsync`/`GetEventsAsync` by root binding rather than adding a service; cost of doing nothing = a contact with Collaborate on a matter cannot see or create its events while the same contact can on a project.</amendment>
    <amendment n="2">COMMUNICATIONS. Keep the communications descriptor this task already plans, with dims on all three roots (verified per step 1). The owner's "same contact access" rule supersedes step 3's default of NOT exposing new modules on CIAM: see amendment 5. Owner round 2 Q6: a communication inherits its PARENT's access permission and its own `sprk_accesspermission` is retired (task 138 owns that change) — this module must not read or honour the communication's own field; Restricted/Limited come from the root.</amendment>
    <amendment n="3">MEMOS (`sprk_memo`). Register a fourth descriptor. design.md §5.1d (`design.md:568`) shows `sprk_memo.sprk_regardingproject`; verify the matter and work-assignment lookups the same way (Notepad's `SUPPORTED_MEMO_PARENTS` names sprk_regardingmatter / sprk_regardingproject / sprk_regardingworkassignment plus event, invoice and budget parents). A memo whose ONLY parent is an event or invoice is reachable by a dim only if it carries the FR-26 core-ancestor stamp; `sprk_memo` is in neither taxonomy set today (`Services/Dataverse/CoreAncestorResolver.cs:56-82`). Task 147 adds it to the CHILD taxonomy (both sides) and backfills memo stamps — memo-on-event/invoice coverage here DEPENDS ON TASK 147 (added to the metadata deps — amendment 9). Memos regarding a project/matter/work assignment directly are covered by the direct columns without waiting.</amendment>
    <amendment n="4">ANALYSES (`sprk_analysis`). Register a fifth descriptor with dims on the three roots (design.md:567 shows sprk_regardingproject; verify matter/work assignment). `sprk_analysis` IS in the CHILD taxonomy (`CoreAncestorResolver.cs:81`), so analyses regarding a child carry the stamp. Project the columns a client may read through a per-module allow-list (task 134, external-module column allow-list) — an analysis row carries AI output fields that must not leak beyond what the SPA renders.</amendment>
    <amendment n="5">PLANES AND LEVEL. "Same contact access as the main record" means: every contact who can read the root on a plane (CIAM and workforce) can read that root's children in these modules, and no contact who cannot read the root can read them. Step 3's "default to NOT adding CIAM exposure" is RETIRED for todo/event/communication/memo/analysis: add the module codes to the CIAM entitlement set (OutsideCounselModules and/or sprk_approlemodulemap per the shipped policy) and record the decision. The child is readable at the contact's level on the root (read-only seam); write routes that exist (to-dos, events per amendment 1) require the same rights on the root as the project routes do. Restricted / deny-list / Secure-direct-only vetoes apply to children exactly as to the root on BOTH planes — coordinate with task 135 (C1 — CIAM veto parity) and task 136 (C2 — rights-based read gates); this task must not reintroduce a presence-only gate (task 070 POML's HasProjectAccess citation is the anti-pattern).</amendment>
    <amendment n="6">DOCUMENTS — THE SECOND PROJECT LOOKUP. The documents module's dims are `sprk_project`, `sprk_matter`, `sprk_workassignment` (`Infrastructure/DI/ExternalAccessModule.cs:250-252`) but `sprk_document` has a SECOND project lookup, `sprk_relatedproject` (design.md:572). A document linked to a project only through it is invisible to that project's contacts. Determine from the data model and the writers what `sprk_relatedproject` means; if it is a parent link, add it as a dim (it may map to the same accessible-project set); if it is a non-access "related" link, record that in the verification table. Escalate if the semantics are ambiguous — it is an access decision.</amendment>
    <amendment n="7">DISCOVERED PARITY GAP — document content, versions and upload exist only under projects (`ExternalProjectDataEndpoints.cs:107`, `:180`, `:193`); a contact with access to a matter or work assignment can list its documents through the module but cannot download or upload them (session26 UC3/UC6 caveats). Review 2026-09-30: no other UAC-r2 task owns it (grep of tasks/ for matter/WA document routes and "UC3/UC6" parity finds only mentions in 134/135/137, none owning the routes), so it IS IN SCOPE here under the same rules as amendment 1 (owner: no deferral), with a §11 justification (existing = the project content/versions/upload routes; extension = generalize by root binding as the to-do routes do; cost of doing nothing = a contact with access to a matter lists its documents but cannot open or add one). Content must come from the ROOT's server-derived container (never client-named), exactly as the project upload route does. If the orchestrator reassigns it before this task starts, record the owning task here.</amendment>
    <amendment n="8">ADDITIONAL ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA (closed set, added to the list above): (a) a contact with access to matter M sees M's events, communications, memos (direct and, after 147, event/invoice-stamped) and analyses; same for a work assignment; (b) a contact WITHOUT access to M sees none of them (0 rows, no query when their root sets are empty); (c) a contact with Collaborate on M can create an event on M through the new matter route and one with View cannot (403, same response shape as the project route); (d) the same contact gets the same child rows on a CIAM token and on a workforce token for the same grants; (e) a Restricted root or a deny-listed contact yields zero child rows on both planes; (f) the verification table records every dim column for the five modules and the `sprk_relatedproject` decision; (g) MANUAL LIVE GATE: an existing test contact granted on a matter and on a work assignment in dev sees their children in the SPA and a contact without the grant does not — recorded; (h) every new external route (amendment 1, and amendment 7 if added) is classified as gated in RouteAuthorizationGuardTests; (i) the communications module returns rows by the ROOT's access permission, never the communication's own `sprk_accesspermission` (test with a communication whose own field disagrees with its root); (j) per amendment 7: a contact with Collaborate on matter M / work assignment W can download, list versions of, and upload a document on M / W, the upload lands in the root's server-derived container, and a contact with View can download but not upload (403) while a contact without access gets the same response as for a non-existent root.</amendment>
    <amendment n="9">ANCHOR DRIFT (review, 2026-09-30). The original body's ExternalAccessModule.cs anchors predate task 028: the documents descriptor is now `:243-254`, the invoices descriptor (step 2's pattern) `:256-268`, and the descriptor registrations span `:208-308` (collaboration `:224-230` through service-requests `:299-308`). Read the file, not the old line numbers. Dependencies 134, 135 and 147 were added to the metadata deps by this amendment; 136 (rights-based read gates) is coordinated, not a dependency — whichever of 056/136 lands second applies the rights gate to the new child routes.</amendment>
  </amendments>
</task>
